### The whole checkout journey, in order: sign up → address → cart → order → pay with Fawaterak → confirmed.
### Send the requests top to bottom (Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code REST Client). Each one uses values
### from the responses before it, so don't skip a step.
###
### Before you start:
###   1. dotnet run --project src/Audiophile.API --launch-profile http
###   2. Fawaterak staging secrets are set (dotnet user-secrets list: Fawaterak:ApiKey, VendorKey, *PaymentMethodId).
###   3. For the REAL webhook (step 9): ngrok http 5040, and Fawaterak:PublicBaseUrl = the ngrok https URL.
###      Without ngrok, Fawaterak can't reach localhost; use step 10 (sync) instead.

@base = http://localhost:5040
# XX59 Headphones (4,499 EGP), seeded by the first migration.
@productId = 4ae5911a-421b-4565-b75f-53809c3da182
# A new user on every run, so the cart starts empty.
@email = buyer.{{$timestamp}}@example.com
@customer = {{signUp.response.body.$.accessToken}}


############################## 1. Sign up (→ 201 with an access token)
# @name signUp
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mona Hassan", "email": "{{email}}", "password": "password-123" }


############################## 2. Save a shipping address (→ 201). The order copies it.
# @name address
POST {{base}}/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullAddressName": "Mona Hassan", "street": "12 Tahrir Street", "city": "Cairo", "country": "Egypt", "phone": "+201000000000", "postalCode": null }


############################## 3. Add to cart (→ 200, the cart with totals)
POST {{base}}/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 1 }


############################## 4. Check the cart before paying
GET {{base}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}


############################## 5. Place the order with Card (→ 201)
# FLOW 1 → 2 → 3 → 4: the API turns the cart into a Pending order, reserves the stock,
# asks Fawaterak for an invoice, and returns payment.checkoutUrl. The cart is now empty.
# @name order
POST {{base}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: card-{{$timestamp}}

{ "addressId": "{{address.response.body.$.id}}", "paymentMethod": "Card" }


############################## 6. Same Idempotency-Key again (→ 200, the SAME order, no second invoice)
POST {{base}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{order.request.headers.Idempotency-Key}}

{ "addressId": "{{address.response.body.$.id}}", "paymentMethod": "Card" }


############################## 7. PAY (FLOW 5): open this URL in your browser
# Copy payment.checkoutUrl from the response of step 5 and open it.
# Staging test card: 5123450000000008 · expiry 12/26 · CVV 100 (any name).
# After paying, Fawaterak redirects the browser to /payments/fawaterak/return (FLOW 9),
# which forwards to the client's orders page. That page doesn't exist until Phase 4: a
# "can't connect" page on localhost:5173 is expected. Check the order in step 8 instead.


############################## 8. Is it paid? (→ status "Confirmed", payment.status "Succeeded")
# With ngrok running, the webhook (FLOW 6 → 7 → 8) has already confirmed it.
# Still "Pending"? The webhook didn't reach you: do step 10.
GET {{base}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}


############################## 9. A forged webhook is refused (→ 401)
# This is what an attacker would send to mark an order paid for free. The hashKey is
# wrong, so FawaterakGateway.ParseWebhookAsync rejects it and nothing changes.
# (The real webhook comes from Fawaterak itself, through ngrok, with a valid hashKey.)
POST {{base}}/payments/fawaterak/webhook_json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invoice_id": 123456,
  "invoice_key": "fake",
  "invoice_status": "paid",
  "payment_method": "Card",
  "pay_load": "{\"order_id\":\"{{order.response.body.$.id}}\"}",
  "hashKey": "not-a-real-signature"
}


############################## 10. Safety net: ask Fawaterak directly (admin only)
# For when the webhook never arrived (no ngrok). Runs the same FLOW 7 lookup + FLOW 8 as a webhook.
# Log in as the admin first (Admin:Email / Admin:Password from `dotnet user-secrets list`).
# @name admin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@audiophile.local", "password": "<Admin:Password from user-secrets>" }

### 10b. Sync the order with Fawaterak (→ the order, Confirmed once Fawaterak says it's paid)
POST {{base}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}/payment/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 10c. Every message Fawaterak sent about this order (the audit trail)
GET {{base}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}/payment/events
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 10d. A customer can't use the support tools (→ 403)
POST {{base}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}/payment/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}


############################## 11. Cash on delivery, for comparison (→ 201, Confirmed at once, no Fawaterak)
# Add something to the cart first (step 3), otherwise → 409 "Your cart is empty."
POST {{base}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: cod-{{$timestamp}}

{ "addressId": "{{address.response.body.$.id}}", "paymentMethod": "CashOnDelivery" }


############################## 12. My orders
GET {{base}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}
